.TH TELEPORT 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
teleport \- Move yourself, a player, or a thing to a destination
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B teleport
.RI [ victim ]
.I destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Move
.I victim
to
.IR destination .
With one argument the victim is you:
.B teleport
.I destination
moves yourself. Both names are matched the way \fBlook\fP and
\fBexamine\fP match them; an unknown name answers that it knows nothing.
.PP
Authority stays with possession: you may move only things you control, into
places you control, with one exception \- a region ruler may move a player
standing in their region. A player victim feels a wrenching sensation when
torn away; anything else just arrives.
.PP
Entities (players and creatures) may only land in rooms; things may land in
anything you control. A destination that resolves to nothing, a move onto
oneself, or a move you are not entitled to make are all refused the same
way.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR room,here,look,examine (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
